-- title:
--   Transport of flatness at p along a Hecke-datum factorisation
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \ge 1$ and a finite set $S$ of primes to be omitted, a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}$, and a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the weight-two Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$) to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$. Let $T_0$ and $T$ be complete local noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebras whose structure maps are local and which are finite free as $\mathcal{O}$-modules, and let $H_0$, $H$ be Hecke–Galois data of type $(N,S,\mathcal{O},\theta)$ over $T_0$ and $T$ respectively: each consists of a Hecke-algebra homomorphism $\pi$ into the ring, reducing to $\theta$ modulo the maximal ideal, with $\mathcal{O}$-algebra generated by the image of $\pi$, such that every Hecke character into $\mathcal{O}$ lifting $\theta$ factors through a point of the ring, with $\mathcal{O}$ surjecting onto the residue field, together with a rank-two adically continuous two-dimensional Galois representation $\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over that ring whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ are $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. Suppose $\varphi : T_0 \to T$ is a local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism with $\varphi \circ H_0.\pi = H.\pi$, and that for a natural number $p$ the representation $H_0.\rho$ satisfies `IsFlatAt p`: the residue field of $T_0$ is finite and, for every ideal $I$ with finite quotient, the finite level $H_0.\rho.V/I$ is isomorphic, compatibly with the Galois action and the group law, to the group of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals with denominator prime to $p$. The conclusion is that there exists a Hecke–Galois datum $H'$ of the same type over $T$ with $H'.\pi = H.\pi$ and $H'.\rho$ flat at $p$ in the same sense.
--
--   This is the step that propagates a finite flat (Fontaine–Laffaille type) condition at $p$ from a Hecke–Galois datum over a smaller deformation-type ring to one over a larger one along a factorisation of the Hecke structure maps; it is used in assembling flat data whose associated primes are controlled by prescribed prime factors, in [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_isFlatAt_of_primeFactors_subset`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_isFlatAt_of_primeFactors_subset).
